A||||17||Patrick's Dad||Creed rocks, man!||||14||
Z||000000||Patrick's Dad||10-30-2001||10:05 PM||||Was in Central Florida for 11 days, up until this morning, and the forum goes to pot. EdBS52 (not his real name) gets booted, there are spiders flying everywhere, and not a single thread devoted to Lisa....<P>Anyway, while we were there, we visited Universal Sudios, where Creed was shooting the video for the first song off "Weathered" (due 11/20), called "My Sacrifice." Too cool.<P>Hopefully, what my Leica lacks in focal length (35mm f2 Summicron ASPH), it makes up in resolution, so's I can blow up the shots I took of Scott Stapp in the water tank. Well, actually, in a small boat in the water in the tank. No wonder "Kongfrontation" was closed.<P>Part two of the story is when my wife and I went back that evening for the Halloween Horror Nights (Not bad, but not as good as six years ago). We hung out like groupies as the tank was replaced by a bus with candles in it (also Scott). A couple of the guys tossed us some Creed guitar picks. I got one. Then one said (not a direct quote): "I have the pick actually used in today's shooting for the person who can name Scott Stapp's son." My wife was the strongest link.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Believe it or not, I'm 36, and haven't hung out with bands in years. I've even met a lot of well known people over the years. I feel like such a groupie. It was still cool.||||reg||14
Z||000001||My7Fieros||10-30-2001||10:20 PM||||I heard a song back in the summer on Rock 103 which is a "classic rock" (and newer stuff to) station here called "My mouth wont open" which was sung to Creeds "With arms wide open"...it was (obviously) a parody of Creed and had references such as "I try to be bet-ter, than Eddie Ve-he-der" (sung as the part of "Welcome to this place, I'll show you everything" in "Arms wide Open". It was talking about how the lead singer of Creed sings through his teeth like Eddie Veder of Pearl Jam. It was a pretty funny song.<BR>Dont get me wrong, I like Creed alot. They rock out for sure! ||||reg||14
Z||000002||Monkeyman||10-31-2001||02:14 AM||||Nothing personal, but you're just now finding out how great Creed is?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I'm 34 (I think--just had a bday, but can't remember [and don't care] what year I was born) and have enjoyed Creeds music since they started.  One thing I like about Creed (especially Scott Stapp) is that he sings about "good" stuff instead of death, violence, rape, guns, etc like most of the popular groups these days.  As a matter of fact, I have both of Creeds CDs right here in my office (at work--still <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ) since my care stereo is currently sitting on my desk at home.  Not too many groups like Creed out there.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Patrick's Dad||10-31-2001||09:09 AM||||Hey Monk,<P>No, we've liked Creed for more than a while. We have both discs, and I'm even on the e-mail list  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Absolutely right about the content of their songs. One of the bands I don't mind my (18 month old) daughter cranking up on the hifi. I also like them musically (Especially "One" and "Torn"), although the mix is a little heavy for my home stereo (A tube preamp and 200wpc MOSFET amp). It's a good thing I didn't get the big woofers...!<P>Right now, the car stereo doesn't like "The Wrong Way" for some reason. I can play anything else on the discs, and I can't see any serious scratches....||||reg||2
Z||000004||Philphine||10-31-2001||09:12 AM||||have you heard the group jars of clay? sorta similar verging on christian rock style.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fogglethorpe||10-31-2001||09:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B>have you heard the group jars of clay? sorta similar verging on christian rock style.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Actually, the first Jars of Clay album ranks as one of my all time favorites. The song "flood" is very moving and powerful.<BR>There seems to be a trend of late in which rock bands are exploring spiritual themes. I agree, Creed is a great band. My wife and I listen to them with our teens.<BR>Also, my daughter is into a band called "Lifehouse", who are not shy about their faith.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||fogglethorpe||10-31-2001||09:35 AM||||Also, check out dcTalk, Third Day, Newsboys, and Delirious.||||reg||1
