Z||000010||MinnGreenGT||10-31-2001||05:18 PM||||If you're into stuff like jars of clay, dcTalk, Third Day, Newsboys, and Delirious... you'd probably be intersted to know that I have a pre-release copy of Petra:Revival sitting on my desk right now...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||10-31-2001||06:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>If you're into stuff like jars of clay, dcTalk, Third Day, Newsboys, and Delirious... you'd probably be intersted to know that I have a pre-release copy of Petra:Revival sitting on my desk right now...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Would you like my address so you can burn and send me a copy?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I've always liked Petra.  Unfortunately, I can't seem to find any of their stuff around here.  All I still have is a cassette of (hmmm...what's the name?  Lots of yellow on the cover).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Patrick's Dad||10-31-2001||08:35 PM||||Thanks for the tip on Lifehouse; Petra's still around???<P>dcTalk: Still haven't found the spark in "Supernatural," but I love "Free at Last" and "Jesus Freak." <P>Newsboys: Kinda the same thing. "Love, Liberty, Disco" is listenable, but not as good as "Going Public" ("Shine" is a great song.), "Take Me to Your Leader," or "Step Up to the Microphone."<P>Also in the category of loving Jars of Clay's first album. "Art in Me" is one of my faves.<P>All this from a Stryper fan of way back. Michael Sweet covered "Always There for You" on his second solo album, but I like the real hard edged tunes, like "More Than a Man," "The Reign," and "Not That Kind of Guy"||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroHeather||11-01-2001||08:58 AM||||Jars of Clay is my absolute fave band, with Third Day close behind.  <P>If ya want the head's up on a really GOOD female artist who's on an indie label, check out <A HREF="http://www.yancynotnancy.com" TARGET=_blank>www.yancynotnancy.com</A>   I ordered Yancy's lil disk, only 6 songs, but I was mesmorized by her voice!  She is really pretty too.<P>Patrick's Dad--Supernatural takes a little getting used to.  It's hard when a band decides to change its style and cater to a different crowd.  Intermission brings back the oldies and adds some flare to their newer stuff too.  I never got into the whole Love Liberty Disco thing.  I stopped at Step Up to the Microphone.<P>Lifehouse and Creed have not publically stood up for which stance they take with their music. The Christian radio station up here wont play either until the bands make a stand as to what they believe as a band.  I still LOVE Lifehouse, and look forward to hearing more of their future projects  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>As for Delierous, their new album is totally not what they were originally about.  It's sad really.  There are a lot of bands out there that sing about "girls" already, we dont need another one.  That's just my $0.02 (USD) worth though.<P>Audio Adrenaline is one of those bands who know how to work a crowd (with their CD or in concert)!  Im excited about checking out their newest album soon  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><sub>Heather is a guru when it comes to the Christian music scene.  Any questions, updates or reviews, dont hesitiate to ask!  No pushing of religion from this girl however  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"></sub>||||reg||1
Z||000014||MinnGreenGT||11-01-2001||10:45 AM||||I work for a portable display company, but the owner used to run a Christain record label.  So we're still pretty well connected in the Christian music scene (had backstage passes for the last Steven Curtis Chapman concert... he's cool to meet.)  I'm even working on a display right now for a new Christian girls pop group <A HREF="http://www.whisperloud.com" TARGET=_blank>Whisper Loud</A>.||||reg||1
Z||000015||fogglethorpe||11-01-2001||04:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroHeather:<BR><B><P>Lifehouse and Creed have not publically stood up for which stance they take with their music. The Christian radio station up here wont play either until the bands make a stand as to what they believe as a band.  I still LOVE Lifehouse, and look forward to hearing more of their future projects   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>[/SUB]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Which "stance"? I think Christian radio stations can't compete with secular stations for precisely that reason...they have to pigeonhole every band, and every business who wants to advertise with them. That makes for serious limitations. Also, I have noticed that, with a few exceptions, (i.e., Jars of Clay), most "Christian" music is either sub-par artistically next to secular music, or indistinguishable from it.<BR>My philosophy is, music is either good or not good, and I find secular and Christian music uplifting.<P>............<BR>Welcome to the religious ghetto....<P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Heretic||11-01-2001||08:01 PM||||I'd Rather Listen to TOOL. But hey , whatever floats your boat. I dont mind the song Higher , Other than that i cant stand Creed.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://shopping.yimg.com/images/muze/album/390/399801_th.jpg">    <BR>TOOL OWNS j00!||||reg||1
Z||000017||FieroHeather||11-03-2001||07:27 AM||||I agree with ya Frogglethorpe that a lot of Christian music is sub-standard.  I absolutely cannot stand it when I invest some money into a CD and it turns out to be crap.  <P>However, there are a lot of bands out there in the Christian music scene that have an excellent sound, and voices that top many of the "best" artists everybody buzzes about.<P>Im my opinion, Rachael Lampa's voice blows Christina Agularia's voice , Mariah Carey's voice and Celine Dion's voice out of the water!  Want a small example, listen to Rachael's song "Blessed" and you will get goosebumps from how beautiful and powerful her voice is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>MinnGreenGT:  I really like Whisper Loud  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  They have some maturing to do as a band, but their initial CD is a fine piece of work.  I also dont mind ZoeGirl or Aurora.  Both of them are in the same genre as WhisperLoud  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
